; The ocaml-protoc-plugin runtime, vendored with its ppx pre-expanded. See
; README.md for why it is vendored rather than depended on -- in short, the
; package's build dependencies make opam-monorepo vendoring impossible, so a
; unikernel could not be built at all.
;
; The library name is not a choice. ocaml-protoc-plugin emits
; `module Runtime' = Ocaml_protoc_plugin` into every generated file, so the
; runtime has to be reachable under exactly that name. The public name is
; web3-codec-protobuf; only the internal library name is fixed.

(library
 (name ocaml_protoc_plugin)
 (public_name web3-codec-protobuf)
 ; Vendored code is not ours to lint. The dev profile promotes warnings to
 ; errors and this trips several by design.
 (flags
  (:standard -w -a))
 ; base64 and ptime are the whole runtime. Note the absence of unix: this
 ; package is linked into Solo5 unikernels, so that must stay true.
 (libraries base64 ptime))
